  "prefLabel": "Ins 206.11 Proposed Findings of Fact and Conclusions of Law",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 206.11 Proposed Findings of Fact and Conclusions of Law.\n\n(a) Any party may submit proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law to the presiding officer prior to or at the hearing.\n\n(b) Upon request of any party, or if the presiding officer determines that proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law would serve to clarify the issues presented at the hearing, the presiding officer shall specify a date for the submission of proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law.\n\n(c) In any case where proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law are submitted, the decision shall include rulings on the proposals.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
